# Line endings are part of this lab's evidence, not a cosmetic detail.
#
# versioning.py hashes the raw bytes of artifacts/system_prompt.md and
# artifacts/tools.yaml to build the artifact_version that every run, transcript
# and version_log row is identified by. Git stores those files with LF, but a
# Windows checkout writes CRLF, which changes the bytes and therefore the hash:
#
#   system_prompt.md as LF   -> fcba1e415b0f
#   the same file as CRLF    -> d0361f9075b2
#
# So the same prompt produced two different artifact_versions depending on who
# checked it out. Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform makes the
# hash a property of the content alone, which is the only way version_log.csv
# is reproducible across the team.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
